From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an Electron app's own schemes are loopback for LNA

Element could not reach a homeserver behind WireGuard. Its pages are at
vector://, an app's own scheme, which has no IP address, so
ChromeContentBrowserClient left it kUnknown and Local Network Access read
it as public. Every request it made to a private address (the VPN's
homeserver, anything on the LAN) was a LOCAL_NETWORK permission request
that neither the app's handler nor the shell is asked about, so it was
never granted.

An app's own scheme is the app, installed on this machine, as
chrome-extension:// is, so it is classed loopback, as the shell is
(patch 0066). Its fetches are then never more private than itself. An
app's http(s) pages are sites and keep LNA as they were.

The schemes are the ones --domicile-electron-schemes registers (patch
0222).

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index 983f7f7..7a5496f 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -2321,6 +2321,18 @@ ChromeContentBrowserClient::DetermineAddressSpaceFromURL(const GURL& url) {
   if (url.SchemeIs(domicile::kDomicileScheme)) {
     return network::mojom::IPAddressSpace::kLoopback;
   }
+  // Domicile's engine fork. An Electron app's own schemes (Element's
+  // vector://) are the app on this machine, not a site, as
+  // chrome-extension:// is. Left kUnknown they read as public, and every
+  // request the app makes into the LAN or a VPN asks for local network access
+  // no one answers.
+  static const base::NoDestructor<std::vector<domicile::ElectronScheme>>
+      electron_schemes(
+          domicile::ElectronSchemesIn(*base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()));
+  if (std::ranges::contains(*electron_schemes, url.scheme(),
+                            &domicile::ElectronScheme::scheme)) {
+    return network::mojom::IPAddressSpace::kLoopback;
+  }
 
   return network::mojom::IPAddressSpace::kUnknown;
 }
